      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOOD'N'YOU (7) has to be close to a victory now. He sat just off them at Newcastle three weeks ago and only just missed. Finds a much softer gate this time. The stable is having a nice trot and bringing him back in trip could see more success. MARCHON (2) came to this course before a break and missed by a nose. If he can just get some fortune early, he could be the strongest one late. CAPTIVATING TYCOON (8) won't be contesting the lead in this but can find the line if last effort is anything to go by. Look for improvement. HARRY'S HALO (5) had two trials to be ready. Definitely one to watch the betting on. PORTICO (6) will be at peak fitness now. The added furlong only looks to be positive into this.",
